      "content": "Thought Process: DP Table"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now that we are all set, let's implement our DP table logic in Python."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Initialize the required variables."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "First, we'll store our item weights and values in lists and also define the capacity of the knapsack."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "# Initialize variables\nw = [2, 3, 6]\nv = [60, 100, 150]\ncapacity = 5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, w is a list of item weights and v is a list of their corresponding values."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. Initialize the DP table."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Then, we create a table with the following dimensions:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "(number of items + 1) x (capacity + 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each cell in this table is initialized to 0."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "content": "# Initialize an empty DP table\nDP = [[0] * (capacity + 1) for _ in range(len(w) + 1)]"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
